\title{h2gam: Automated GAM Covariate Validation and Selection for 'mgcv'}
\description{
Given a response and a pool of candidate covariates, profiles the response and auto-suggests an 'mgcv' family (count / proportion / positive / gaussian branches, ranked by AIC and residual diagnostics), forward-selects a decorrelated, prediction-relevant covariate subset scored by spatial-block or response-stratified cross-validation with a concurvity gate and a BIC tie-break / one-standard-error stopping rule, then runs a bidirectional backward re-check and a final shrinkage fit with adequacy diagnostics. Structural (spatial/temporal) terms are forced in and not screened, so covariates must earn their place over and above them.
